WEBVTT

1
00:00:43.125 --> 00:00:47.000
In verses 17.2 to 17.4 of Chapter 17,

2
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.166
Lord Krishna describes those people who,
due to laziness or difficulty,

3
00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:55.416
are unable to fully follow the scriptures.

4
00:00:55.416 --> 00:00:57.625
Yet they keep faith

5
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:00.250
and continue to worship the deities.

6
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.750
Their practice is not scripturally sanctioned,

7
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.958
but at some level it is connected to belief.

8
00:01:05.958 --> 00:01:09.125
But in verses 17.5 and 17.6, Lord Krishna

9
00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:10.666
points toward a completely

10
00:01:10.666 --> 00:01:13.625
different class of people.

11
00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:16.916
These people do not merely abandon scripture,

12
00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:19.458
but oppose it as well.

13
00:01:19.458 --> 00:01:23.333
They adopt severe and
unsanctioned austerities –

14
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:24.791
which are driven by pride,

15
00:01:24.791 --> 00:01:28.541
ego, and distorted desires.

16
00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:29.625
Through such conduct

17
00:01:29.625 --> 00:01:32.166
they cause suffering to their own body,

18
00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:33.750
and also give pain

19
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.375
to the Paramatma dwelling within.

20
00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:37.916
This is why Lord Krishna

21
00:01:37.916 --> 00:01:39.291
describes them – going beyond ignorance –

22
00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:43.208
as directly having a demonic disposition.

23
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.375
In verses 17.5 and 17.6 of Chapter 17,
Lord Krishna

24
00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:54.500
discusses those people

25
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:58.250
who adopt severe and unsanctioned austerities.

26
00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.375
They keep harsh fasts,

27
00:02:00.375 --> 00:02:02.583
perform painful rituals,

28
00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:06.000
or invent rules that torment the body.

29
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.291
But all of this they do not

30
00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:12.041
out of humility or devotion, but driven by ego,

31
00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:16.250
pride, and the craving for power or fame.

32
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.500
From the outside their conduct may look spiritual –

33
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.708
such as giving up food or difficult practice.

34
00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:25.041
But if this is only show,

35
00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:28.125
or a means of impressing others,

36
00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:29.458
then instead of lifting

37
00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:33.041
the soul higher, it drags it further down.

38
00:02:33.041 --> 00:02:35.833
Such people leave the boundaries of scripture

39
00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:37.916
and create their own methods.

40
00:02:37.916 --> 00:02:42.875
They torment their body – which
is made of the five great elements –

41
00:02:42.875 --> 00:02:44.250
and also give pain

42
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.166
to the Paramatma seated within.

43
00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:49.541
This is why they are called not spiritual heroes, 

44
00:02:49.541 --> 00:02:52.666
but driven by a demonic tendency.

45
00:02:52.666 --> 00:02:54.250
The outer covering

46
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.458
of their discipline actually draws its power

47
00:02:56.458 --> 00:02:59.583
from ego and desire.

48
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:02.333
Here there is a deep teaching –

49
00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:05.416
austerity in itself is not faulty.

50
00:03:05.416 --> 00:03:08.125
Fasting or discipline done with the right feeling

51
00:03:08.125 --> 00:03:11.375
concentrates the mind,

52
00:03:11.375 --> 00:03:13.041
purifies the soul,

53
00:03:13.041 --> 00:03:16.083
and connects the seeker with God.

54
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:20.625
But when that same austerity
begins to feed the ego,

55
00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:24.291
or becomes a means of controlling
others, then it

56
00:03:24.291 --> 00:03:27.333
no longer has any spiritual value.

57
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:29.166
This illustration is found

58
00:03:29.166 --> 00:03:31.125
in history and in the scriptures too.

59
00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:34.083
In the Ramayana, the asuras
performed severe austerity,

60
00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:37.833
but their aim was only to gain
power and dominance.

61
00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.000
Their practice looked spiritual

62
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.541
from the outside, but within

63
00:03:41.541 --> 00:03:44.541
it was driven by distortion and ego.

64
00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:46.958
This is why Lord Krishna reminds us –

65
00:03:46.958 --> 00:03:50.625
everything that looks spiritual from the outside

66
00:03:50.625 --> 00:03:53.750
does not actually give spiritual progress.

67
00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:58.500
True practice is only that which is done
within the boundaries of scripture,

68
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.708
with humility and love.

69
00:04:06.458 --> 00:04:11.208
Your discipline may look very impressive
from the outside –

70
00:04:11.208 --> 00:04:15.041
waking up early in the morning,
keeping long fasts,

71
00:04:15.041 --> 00:04:20.375
practising silence for hours, or
following strict rules.

72
00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:21.958
But

73
00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:25.291
pause a little and ask yourself –

74
00:04:25.291 --> 00:04:29.583
is this nourishing your soul,

75
00:04:29.583 --> 00:04:34.916
or only feeding your ego?

76
00:04:34.916 --> 00:04:38.541
Discipline does not mean punishing the body;

77
00:04:38.541 --> 00:04:42.208
its purpose is to purify the heart.

78
00:04:42.208 --> 00:04:46.500
If your practice is making you
more compassionate, steady,

79
00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.041
and humble,

80
00:04:48.041 --> 00:04:50.916
then understand that it is in the right direction.

81
00:04:50.916 --> 00:04:54.416
But if that same practice is making you irritable, harsh,

82
00:04:54.416 --> 00:04:55.958
or someone who considers

83
00:04:55.958 --> 00:04:58.708
themselves superior to others,

84
00:04:58.708 --> 00:05:01.875
then it is not the spiritual path –

85
00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:05.541
it is leading toward ego.

86
00:05:05.541 --> 00:05:07.916
Remember,

87
00:05:07.916 --> 00:05:13.958
I dwell within you as the Paramatma.

88
00:05:13.958 --> 00:05:18.500
When you give your body
unnecessary suffering,

89
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:23.916
or move away from compassion
through your practice,

90
00:05:23.916 --> 00:05:27.750
then you give pain to Me too.

91
00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:32.875
Do not mistake outer effort for inner progress.

92
00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.333
True practice

93
00:05:35.333 --> 00:05:38.416
makes you lighter, not heavier.

94
00:05:38.416 --> 00:05:41.125
It calms the mind, it does not harden it.

95
00:05:41.125 --> 00:05:42.666
So the next time

96
00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:46.708
you adopt any discipline, be sure to see this –

97
00:05:46.708 --> 00:05:49.083
is it making you calm

98
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:51.416
and loving from within?

99
00:05:51.416 --> 00:05:55.291
If yes, then this austerity is pure.

100
00:06:00.041 --> 00:06:02.375
In your home, your children

101
00:06:02.375 --> 00:06:06.416
and family members are quietly watching

102
00:06:06.416 --> 00:06:10.208
how you live out your values.

103
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:11.333
If they see

104
00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:14.208
that you keep harsh fasts or do difficult

105
00:06:14.208 --> 00:06:17.833
practices only for pride or show,

106
00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.375
then they will learn to associate spirituality

107
00:06:20.375 --> 00:06:23.625
not with ease, but with harshness.

108
00:06:23.625 --> 00:06:27.500
Now pause and think –

109
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:32.166
what are you handing over to
the next generation?

110
00:06:32.166 --> 00:06:35.000
Humility, or only habits?

111
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.000
Discipline,

112
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.166
when done with compassion and simplicity,

113
00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:43.000
becomes a living example.

114
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:43.916
But when that same

115
00:06:43.916 --> 00:06:48.583
discipline is filled with superiority or guilt,

116
00:06:48.583 --> 00:06:51.125
then it becomes a burden –

117
00:06:51.125 --> 00:06:54.500
pressed down by the unseen weight of traditions!

118
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.791
Your children

119
00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:57.666
do not need to see

120
00:06:57.666 --> 00:07:00.541
how much suffering you can give yourself.

121
00:07:00.541 --> 00:07:03.000
They need to see –

122
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.041
how deeply can you connect
with the Paramatma?

123
00:07:07.041 --> 00:07:11.333
Make your practice gentle and meaningful.

124
00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:12.541
When the worship in the home

125
00:07:12.541 --> 00:07:15.000
is filled with love and peace,

126
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.500
and traditions are carried
out with understanding,

127
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.416
then it lifts the spiritual atmosphere
of the home.

128
00:07:22.416 --> 00:07:27.000
And this very atmosphere carries
forward into the future too –

129
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.583
not from fear, but from love and light.

130
00:07:36.375 --> 00:07:39.083
In the workplace, people often take harsh

131
00:07:39.083 --> 00:07:42.333
discipline itself to be dedication –

132
00:07:42.333 --> 00:07:45.708
giving up sleep and food, late

133
00:07:45.708 --> 00:07:47.000
into the night replying to emails,

134
00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.875
or staying constantly immersed in work.

135
00:07:49.875 --> 00:07:52.833
From the outside all this may
look like ‘commitment,’

136
00:07:52.833 --> 00:07:54.541
but

137
00:07:54.541 --> 00:07:58.000
in reality it can also be self-harm.

138
00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.708
In this verse

139
00:07:59.708 --> 00:08:03.416
I mention those people who perform severe

140
00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:07.916
austerity out of ego and pride.

141
00:08:07.916 --> 00:08:12.250
A similar tendency can be seen
at the workplace too –

142
00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.041
where people neglect their health,

143
00:08:14.041 --> 00:08:17.875
mental peace, and relationships,

144
00:08:17.875 --> 00:08:21.458
and run only after name and achievement.

145
00:08:21.458 --> 00:08:25.500
This culture may be praised from the outside,

146
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:28.833
but from within it exhausts you,

147
00:08:28.833 --> 00:08:33.791
burdens the mind, and takes you
away from joy.

148
00:08:33.791 --> 00:08:37.250
This tendency of yours at the workplace

149
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.791
also becomes a cause

150
00:08:38.791 --> 00:08:41.833
of inconvenience for your colleagues.

151
00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:45.375
In truth, there is a difference

152
00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:49.916
as vast as earth and sky between being sincere

153
00:08:49.916 --> 00:08:52.583
and acting out the show of being sincere.

154
00:08:52.583 --> 00:08:54.541
Remember,

155
00:08:54.541 --> 00:08:59.166
I dwell within you as the Paramatma.

156
00:08:59.166 --> 00:09:01.875
When you, in the name of success,

157
00:09:01.875 --> 00:09:05.541
give suffering to your body and mind,

158
00:09:05.541 --> 00:09:08.958
then you push Me away too.

159
00:09:08.958 --> 00:09:11.000
True professional discipline

160
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.500
lifts the soul higher, it does not suppress it.

161
00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:19.583
So choose purpose instead of performance.

162
00:09:19.583 --> 00:09:22.666
Only then does your work become worship,

163
00:09:22.666 --> 00:09:25.833
and your practice becomes not merely

164
00:09:25.833 --> 00:09:29.708
achievement, but a path of real growth.
